<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The pre-cutover half of a matched pair. Filed before 2023-01-03, so every
  <value> here is THOUSANDS of dollars.

  information_table_dollars.xml reports the same four positions - same CUSIPs,
  same share counts, the same money - as a filing submitted after the cutover,
  where the same figures are written in whole dollars and are therefore 1000x
  larger. Neither document says which convention it uses; only filed_at does.

  The pair exists so that "the same position, filed on either side of the line,
  normalises to the same number of dollars" is a test rather than an intention.
  Do not change a value in one file without changing the other by exactly 1000x,
  or the property under test becomes untestable and the suite will say so.

  The share counts are round and the implied prices are deliberately ordinary -
  $170.00, $340.00, $60.00, $5.00. The last one is the interesting one: at $5 a
  share, reading this document as whole dollars implies a price of half a cent,
  which is what the implied-price guard is calibrated to catch.
-->
